# Render Static Site routing (Netlify-style _redirects).
#
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# IMPORTANT: This file is DEPLOYED but NON-FUNCTIONAL on Render.
# Render's static-site _redirects parser does NOT apply SPA-fallback
# rules (200-status rewrites) for paths that don't exist as real files.
# The rules below are here for documentation + future migration to
# Netlify/Vercel where they WILL work.
#
# The ACTUAL SPA fallback is handled by /404.html — a custom error
# page that IS the Flutter app shell. When a user reloads a deep link
# like /pointOfSale, Render serves 404.html (the Flutter shell) and
# the Flutter router handles the route. See build.sh step 4c.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# build.sh copies this file into build/web/_redirects after flutter build.
/    /index.html   200
/*    /app.html   200
